WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.115
Install the SDK, and know which version you have.

2
00:00:03.395 --> 00:00:06.851
The official Python SDK is the mcp package.

3
00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:19.739
Its v2 line, released in July 2026, supports the stateless 2026-07-28 revision and still serves older clients from the same server.

4
00:00:20.019 --> 00:00:30.237
Install it with the CLI extra, which adds the mcp command: pip install "mcp[cli]" (or uv add "mcp[cli]" in a uv project).

5
00:00:30.517 --> 00:00:32.224
Two version facts save hours.

6
00:00:32.504 --> 00:00:40.099
First, v2 renamed the high-level class: FastMCP is now MCPServer, imported from mcp.

7
00:00:40.379 --> 00:00:41.125
server.

8
00:00:41.405 --> 00:00:50.984
The decorator API is otherwise the same, so most v1 examples translate directly, but code that imports FastMCP is v1 code.

9
00:00:51.264 --> 00:00:55.765
Second, v1 is in maintenance mode, receiving only security fixes.

10
00:00:56.045 --> 00:01:02.680
If you inherit a v1 server, pin it below 2 until you migrate, and read the SDK’s migration guide.

11
00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:07.525
The SDK’s central idea is that your function signature is the schema.

12
00:01:07.805 --> 00:01:20.179
Type hints become JSON Schema types, defaults make parameters optional, Literal becomes an enum, and Annotated with Pydantic’s Field adds descriptions and constraints such as minimum and maximum.

13
00:01:20.459 --> 00:01:22.784
The docstring becomes the tool description.

14
00:01:23.064 --> 00:01:31.363
The SDK validates every call’s arguments against that schema before your function runs, so a wrong type never reaches your code.

15
00:01:31.643 --> 00:01:37.872
Your job is the checks a schema cannot express: does this issue exist, is this status change allowed.
